.TH SH-DOCS 1 "2026-10-19" "sh-docs 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sh\-docs \- generate Markdown API documentation from shell doc comments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sh\-docs
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fIFILE\fR]
.br
.B sh\-docs
.B \-\-output\-dir
\fIDIR\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]... \fIFILE\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sh\-docs
reads a shell script and writes GitHub\-flavored Markdown describing it.
It parses the annotations in the file header and in the comment block above
each function definition, and renders a document with a navigation block, an
overview, a highlight list of the documented functions, and a reference section
with tables for arguments, options, environment variables, exit codes and
streams.
.PP
\fIFILE\fR defaults to standard input, which can also be named
.BR \- ,
and the document is written to standard
output unless
.B \-\-output
is given.
.PP
The annotation language is documented in the project README. In short, the file
header takes
.BR @file / @name ,
.BR @brief ,
.BR @description ,
.BR @usage ,
.BR @env ,
.BR @see ,
.BR @tip ,
.BR @deprecated ,
.BR @license ,
.B @since
and
.BR @namespace ,
plus the command line and examples of a script:
.BR @option ,
.BR @arg ,
.BR @stdin ,
.BR @stdout ,
.BR @stderr ,
.B @exitcode
and
.BR @example .
A function takes
.BR @description ,
.BR @section ,
.BR @example ,
.BR @arg ,
.BR @option ,
.BR @env ,
.BR @set ,
.BR @exitcode ,
.BR @stdin ,
.BR @stdout ,
.BR @stderr ,
.BR @noargs ,
.BR @note ,
.BR @tip ,
.BR @see ,
.BR @deprecated ,
.BR @warning ,
.B @since
and
.BR @internal .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write the document to \fIFILE\fR instead of standard output.
.TP
.BR \-\-output\-dir " \fIDIR\fR"
Write one document per \fIFILE\fR into \fIDIR\fR, named after it with a
\fB.sh\fR, \fB.bash\fR, \fB.zsh\fR or \fB.ksh\fR extension dropped. Any number
of \fIFILE\fRs can be given, and standard input cannot.
.TP
.B \-\-index
With \fB\-\-output\-dir\fR, also write \fIDIR\fB/index.md\fR, listing the
documents with their brief.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Compare the document with the one already in the \fB\-\-output\fR file, byte
for byte, instead of writing it. When that file is missing or differs, print a
unified diff on standard output, name the file on standard error, and exit 1.
The file is never written. Requires \fB\-\-output\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Report every tag sh\-docs does not know, every public function without
\fB@description\fR, and every \fB$\fIN\fR a public function reads without an
\fB@arg $\fIN\fR, on standard error with its line number. The document is
written all the same, and the exit status is 1. A function whose name, or the
last \fB::\fR part of it, starts with \fB_\fR is private and needs no
description.
.TP
.BR \-\-format " \fIFORMAT\fR"
\fBmarkdown\fR, the default, or \fBman\fR for a roff man page with the
conventional sections, and the functions of a library under FUNCTIONS.
.TP
.BR \-\-man\-section " \fIN\fR"
The section of a man page, 1 by default. Under \fB\-\-output\-dir\fR it is also
the extension of each page.
.TP
.BR \-\-man\-date " \fIDATE\fR"
The date in the header of a man page. There is none by default, so a page
generated twice is the same both times.
.TP
.B \-\-line\-links
Link each function to the line it is declared on. Off by default, since any
edit above a function moves its line.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-emoji
Print every heading, label and callout without its emoji.
.TP
.BR \-\-src\-dir " \fIDIR\fR"
Directory the documented sources live in. Default: \fBsrc\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-doc\-dir " \fIDIR\fR"
Directory the generated documents live in, used to resolve relative links.
Default: \fBdocs\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-root\-files " \fILIST\fR"
Comma\-separated sources that sit at the repository root instead of inside
\fB\-\-src\-dir\fR. Default: \fBinit.sh\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-source\-path " \fIPATH\fR"
Path of the documented source relative to the repository root. Overrides
\fB\-\-src\-dir\fR and \fB\-\-root\-files\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-link\-dirs " \fILIST\fR"
Comma\-separated path prefixes that \fB@see\fR entries are resolved as paths
rather than as anchors. Default: \fBdocs,example,src,scripts\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-example\-dir " \fIDIR\fR"
Scan \fIDIR\fR for example scripts that mention a documented function and list
them under "Related examples". Scanning is off by default.
.TP
.BR \-\-example\-prefix " \fIDIR\fR"
Prefix the scanned examples are linked under. Default: \fBexample\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SH_DOCS_AWK
Path of the awk program. Defaults to
.I sh\-docs.awk
next to the
.B sh\-docs
script.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The documents were generated, and \fB\-\-check\fR and \fB\-\-strict\fR found
nothing.
.TP
.B 1
\fB\-\-check\fR found a document missing or out of date, or \fB\-\-strict\fR
reported a problem.
.TP
.B 2
The invocation was invalid, an input could not be read, or awk failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate a document for one module:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sh\-docs < src/strings.sh > docs/strings.md
.fi
.RE
.PP
Document a module that lives outside the default layout:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sh\-docs \-\-source\-path lib/text/strings.sh lib/text/strings.sh \-o docs/strings.md
.fi
.RE
.PP
Fail a CI job when a committed document has fallen behind its source:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sh\-docs \-\-check src/strings.sh \-o docs/strings.md
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gawk (1),
.BR shdoc (1)
